<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        ValidationRule.Description is capped at 255 characters. The rationale below is
        operationally important, so it was moved here rather than trimmed; a comment is
        repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata API. Do not paste this back into
        <description>. NOTE ALSO: the comment must sit INSIDE the root element - a comment
        placed ABOVE <ValidationRule> breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        THE WIRE GATE. A disposition cannot be marked Completed while the wire-fraud check
        is incomplete. Wire_Verification_Completed__c is DERIVED - the Wire_Verification_Rollup
        flow sets it from the MOST RECENT Wire__c on the disposition (the same row
        WireSelector.selectMostRecentByDispositionId returns), true only when all six
        confirmation fields are populated.

        WHY THIS SHAPE, NOT AN APPROVAL entryCriteria (design Q4):
        Putting the flag in Closing_Approval's entryCriteria would surface an unmet gate as
        the platform's "no applicable approval process was found" - a misleading error the
        user cannot act on. Instead the flag is an approvalPageFields entry on
        Closing_Approval so the approver SEES the wire state when deciding, and the hard stop
        lives here where its message renders natively in the Path UI.

        WHY OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(...)):
        ISCHANGED alone gates the transition but leaves a create-at-Completed hole. ISNEW
        closes it. Together they still do NOT trap rows already sitting at Completed, whose
        every subsequent edit would otherwise be blocked. Same shape as the deployed
        Property_Registry__c.Winning_Lead_Required.

        🔴 THE FIRING SURFACE IS NO LONGER CLEAN - RETRACTED 2026-08-09 BY TRANCHE 3C, AND THE
        FORMULA BELOW DID NOT CHANGE. The superseded sentences are quoted and retracted rather
        than deleted, because a stale "nothing but user edits" premise is exactly the kind of
        thing a future reader keeps reasoning from:

            RETRACTED: "FIRING SURFACE IS CLEAN. Disposition_Stage__c is written by nothing but
            user edits - the Path, the Details section and inline edit. No Apex, no flow and no
            approval field update writes it."

        WHAT REPLACED IT: DISPOSITION_STAGE__C NOW HAS TWO WRITERS. (1) User edits, as before:
        the Path, the Details section and inline edit. (2) ContractExecutionService's disposition
        arm, advanceDispositionsToClosing, which writes Disposition_Stage__c = 'Closing' when a
        sell-side PSA reaches Executed on the related Contract Review. It is the first machine
        writer of this field in the application. Still true: no flow and no approval field update
        writes it.

        WHAT IT MEANS FOR THIS RULE: NOTHING IN THE LOGIC, ONLY IN THE PREMISE. This rule guards
        the Closing to Completed transition. The new writer moves records INTO Closing and never
        out of it, and it never writes Completed, so it cannot satisfy the
        ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, 'Completed') term and cannot trip this gate. Both
        ISNEW() and ISCHANGED(Disposition_Stage__c) are unaffected. Contrast the sibling rule
        All_NDAs_Signed_Before_Progression, which gates 'Closing' itself and therefore CAN now
        fire against a write no human made; its comment carries that analysis.

        THE APPROVAL POINT SURVIVES, ON ITS OWN REASONING RATHER THAN ON THE RETRACTED ONE. The
        three Disposition approval processes still carry NO finalApprovalActions, because an
        approval field update would bypass validation rules entirely. That is independent of the
        new writer, which is ordinary DML: this rule DOES evaluate against the machine write (it
        simply cannot be tripped by it, per the paragraph above).

        DEPLOY ORDER - LOAD-BEARING. The Wire_Verification_Rollup flow MUST be deployed
        BEFORE this rule. Deploying the rule first leaves Wire_Verification_Completed__c false
        everywhere with nothing able to set it, so NO disposition could reach Completed.

        BLAST RADIUS OF ISNEW() - for the developer and testing agents. Any existing test or
        seed script that INSERTS a Disposition__c directly at Completed will start failing.
        Sweep TestDataFactory.createDispositions, DispositionSelectorTest,
        DispositionControllerTest, BovControllerTest, WireServiceTest, WireControllerTest and
        the disposition seed scripts.
    -->
    <fullName>Wire_Complete_Before_Completed</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Blocks the Closing to Completed transition (and create-at-Completed) while Wire_Verification_Completed__c is false. That flag is derived by the Wire_Verification_Rollup flow. See the XML comment in this file for full rationale.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, &apos;Completed&apos;),
    OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(Disposition_Stage__c)),
    NOT(Wire_Verification_Completed__c)
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorDisplayField>Disposition_Stage__c</errorDisplayField>
    <errorMessage>The wire verification is not complete. All six wire confirmation fields must be confirmed on the Wire record before this disposition can be marked Completed.</errorMessage>
</ValidationRule>
